KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ recursion reached depth 2: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
A class template partial specialization whose last argument is a pack
expansion T... must match an instantiation with at least as many arguments as
the specialization has non-pack parameters, binding the trailing arguments to
the pack.  Currently the matcher requires an exact count, so for two or more
trailing-pack elements the recursive partial spec is skipped, the primary is
selected, the recursion stops and main is truncated.  Flip to CORE once
trailing-pack partial-spec matching is implemented.
